## Original Content
Five political parties have won seats in Kazakhstan's first election to the country's new unicameral parliament, the Kurultai, according to preliminary results released on Monday by the Central Election Commission.

## Summary
Kazakhstan held its first election to its new unicameral parliament, the Kurultai. Five political parties won seats according to preliminary results released by the Central Election Commission on Monday.

## Key Points
- First election to Kazakhstan's unicameral parliament, the Kurultai.
- Five political parties secured seats based on preliminary results.
- Results were announced by the Central Election Commission.
- This election represents a change in Kazakhstan's legislative structure.


